    <string name="about_game">About the game</string>
    <string name="parent_help">Maths practice is optional. Turn it off in Settings to play chess without maths or breaks. With maths on, start with five minutes of maths and at least three correct answers. Finish the current exercise. Then take a one-minute break. Chess starts automatically. Finish the chess game. Then continue with maths.\n\nOnly time in the visible, active app counts. Menus and pauses stop the timer. The break timer runs only on the break screen. A correct answer with a hint also counts. The app cannot measure whether a child is thinking.\n\nThe app does not detect every dead position. In rare blocked positions, play can continue even though neither player can give checkmate.\n\nThe computer calculates its moves on the TV. Its playing strength and learning effect have not been established.</string>
